3.7.2. Method 2: Soft Voting Ensemble Learning
The Soft Voting Ensemble Learning (Method 2) (depicted as Soft Voting Classification in Figure 1) considers the class prediction probabilities of each base learner and combines these predictions through an average function to perform the final classification. In general, there are two voting Ensemble Learning methods: a) Majority Voting [55] and b) Soft Voting [56], which differ on the way they process the results in the fusion model. Particularly, the Majority Voting takes the output of the base learners and performs the final classification based on the majority votes, while Soft Voting, averages the decisions of each base learner to perform the final classification. In this way, when compared with Majority Voting, the Soft Voting method eliminates the structure sensitivity that occurs from the base learners, reduces the ensemble’s variance, and obtains more information.
